+# Incidents brief: August–September 2026
+
+Action status as of the 30 September on-call sync.
+
+## 11 August 2026: ingest backlog and full database disk
+
+**Impact:** Overnight, incoming data stalled for about two and a half hours. Customers saw stale dashboards; no data was lost.
+
+**Cause:** One malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; the retry logs filled the database disk until writes were refused.
+
+**Fix:** A restart that set the bad batch aside, then non-blocking space reclamation and log cleanup.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done.
+- Fix so bad batches cannot jam ingest (Jonas): open, in review.
+- Paging escalation rules (Elif): done; unanswered pages escalate after 15 minutes.
+
+## 21 September 2026: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** The public API was down for 47 minutes; nearly all clients failed to connect.
+
+**Cause:** The certificate's automatic renewal had failed silently for weeks after a credential change.
+
+**Fix:** Certificate renewed and API restarted; renewal failures now raise an alert.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Reminder 14 days before expiry (Priya): done.
+- Alert on days left (Priya): open.
+- Certificate check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+- Handlers record their steps during incidents (Mara): done.
